<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Hungarian Honvéd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal Hungarian Honvéd was the territorial army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, created in 1868 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a>, with Hungarian as its language of command. Its name recalled the Hungarian revolutionary army of 1848–1849. Like the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landwehr">Landwehr</a> it grew into a front-line force and fought throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-hungarian-honved.jpg" alt="Royal Hungarian Honvéd" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felipe Fidelis Tobias · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colors_of_the_Royal_Hungarian_Honv%C3%A9d.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
